            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/error_codes.hpp",
                    "line": 25,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jinu Joy Thomas",
                        "email": "jinu.joy.thomas@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jinuthomas"
                    },
                    "message": "since you are using these why don't you make it \nDEVICE_NOT_PRESENT\nDEVICE_PRESENCE_UNKNOWN  \nGPIO_LINE_EXCEPTION"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/error_codes.hpp",
                    "line": 25,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "GPIO_LINE_EXCEPTION is already there.\n\nDEVICE_NOT_PRESENT - won't be ambiguous? When to set that error code, when it was concluded based on file missing or when it was concluded based on presence pin returning false?\n\nDEVICE_PRESENCE_UNKNOWN - This condition will be automatically deduced by the caller based on error code returned by the utility API? \nLets say that caller gets an error code other than \"PRESENCE_PIN_READ_FALSE\" at its end, this itself implies there was some other exception and hence presence is unknown?\nDo this make sense or you have some other thought here?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/error_codes.hpp",
                    "line": 25,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "> Do ~ Does"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/error_codes.hpp",
                    "line": 25,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jinu Joy Thomas",
                        "email": "jinu.joy.thomas@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jinuthomas"
                    },
                    "message": "instead of PRESENCE_PIN_READ_FALSE make it DEVICE_NOT_PRESENT \nfor GPIO exception on presence lest have the code as DEVICE_PRESENCE_UNKNOWN\nand for other generic GPIO exceptions for not related to presence lets have GPIO_LINE_EXCEPTION. This will be more readable and understandable to follow code for future folks"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/error_codes.hpp",
                    "line": 25,
                    "reviewer": {
